WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.562 --> 00:00:15.423
Zann gulped.

2
00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:18.304
Wyssa didn't have a plan to find Morb!

3
00:00:18.865 --> 00:00:20.205
It was a strange thought.

4
00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.327
Wyssa usually knew everything.

5
00:00:22.827 --> 00:00:24.648
Perda looked stunned for a second too.

6
00:00:25.168 --> 00:00:26.769
Then she cleared her throat.

7
00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:31.884
"I've read every word of Zann's parents' books," she told Wyssa.

8
00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:36.348
"In the one about the Far Frontier, they talked about how hard it was to walk on the

9
00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:37.289
shifting sand."

10
00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:39.791
"Yes, and what's your point?"

11
00:00:40.351 --> 00:00:41.632
Wyssa sounded irritated.

12
00:00:41.652 --> 00:00:44.234
"We can't zap while we're here.

13
00:00:44.595 --> 00:00:46.276
The magic is too unpredictable."

14
00:00:46.996 --> 00:00:50.539
"Nax and Asta befriended some of the nomads who live here."

15
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.322
Perda waved a hand at the desert surrounding them.

16
00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:57.725
"The nomads taught them to summon something called a hoof beast."

17
00:00:57.745 --> 00:00:59.787
"A hoof beast?"

18
00:01:00.127 --> 00:01:00.828
Gliss echoed.

19
00:01:01.332 --> 00:01:02.113
"What's that?"

20
00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:05.075
"It's a native desert animal," Darb said.

21
00:01:05.095 --> 00:01:06.536
"I've read about them."

22
00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:08.357
Perda nodded.

23
00:01:08.377 --> 00:01:13.501
"The nomads taught Zann's parents to control them using just a little bit of magic.

24
00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:17.143
That way they could ride them instead of fighting the sand."

25
00:01:17.163 --> 00:01:18.544
"Of course."

26
00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.225
Wyssa cleared her throat.

27
00:01:20.245 --> 00:01:24.348
"I was just going to suggest summoning a few of those beasts."

28
00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:26.830
Zann traded a look with his friends.

29
00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.312
Had Wyssa really planned to suggest that?

30
00:01:30.252 --> 00:01:31.453
He decided it didn't matter.

31
00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:35.436
Wyssa was already pulling some dried leaves and twigs out of her pockets.

32
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:40.079
Whether it was her idea or not, she seemed to know how to summon the beasts.

33
00:01:40.839 --> 00:01:43.301
"Hold out your hands," Wyssa ordered the kids.

34
00:01:43.321 --> 00:01:46.563
"Create friction while I sprinkle this on you.

35
00:01:47.123 --> 00:01:48.404
But be careful."

36
00:01:49.085 --> 00:01:51.006
Zann and his friends did as she said.

37
00:01:51.806 --> 00:01:54.368
Soon magic energy was sparking around them.

38
00:01:55.068 --> 00:02:00.052
Wyssa muttered under her breath and closed her eyes, waving her hands to direct the energy.

39
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:07.302
"Whoa." Perda blinked as a tiny spark exploded in front of her eyes.

40
00:02:07.322 --> 00:02:09.023
"This is crazy."

41
00:02:09.523 --> 00:02:10.203
Gliss nodded.

42
00:02:10.223 --> 00:02:15.125
"It reminds me of the unstable energy near the Cave of the Unknown."

43
00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:21.068
Zann glanced at Wyssa, but she was ignoring them as she continued to murmur and wave her hands.

44
00:02:21.088 --> 00:02:25.830
"Maybe there's a powerful source of magic near here too," he said to his friends.

45
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:27.550
Gliss gasped.

46
00:02:28.011 --> 00:02:29.671
"Like the Source?"

47
00:02:30.392 --> 00:02:31.092
Zann nodded.

48
00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:33.649
"What if that's why Morb came here?

49
00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:35.509
Maybe he's trying to find it."

50
00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:39.030
"And control it," Perda added grimly.

51
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.712
"And I thought it was scary when it was only Laddno who wanted to find the Source!"

52
00:02:43.732 --> 00:02:47.893
"The Source might not even exist," Gliss said.

53
00:02:48.354 --> 00:02:51.935
Before Zann could respond, he heard thundering hooves in the distance.

54
00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:55.636
Half a dozen strange creatures appeared on the horizon.

55
00:02:56.416 --> 00:03:01.719
They stopped some distance away and peered at the humans with large, dark eyes.

56
00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:05.121
"Are those hoof beasts?"

57
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:06.221
Gliss whispered.

58
00:03:06.842 --> 00:03:07.602
Darb nodded.

59
00:03:07.622 --> 00:03:10.564
"They look just like the pictures in the book I read."

60
00:03:11.204 --> 00:03:14.366
Perda took a step forward, shading her eyes for a better look.

61
00:03:14.386 --> 00:03:19.609
"They look sort of like desert donkeys, but bigger," she said.

62
00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:22.330
"Prettier too," Gliss put in.

63
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.252
"Look at their long manes and tails!"

64
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.181
Zann had to agree.

65
00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:32.203
The beasts had multicolored hair in shades of gold, brown, and yellow.

66
00:03:32.223 --> 00:03:36.224
"Their hair helps them blend into the desert," Darb said.

67
00:03:36.244 --> 00:03:40.246
"And those wide hooves help them get traction in the shifting sand."

68
00:03:41.066 --> 00:03:41.826
Wyssa frowned.

69
00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:44.487
"Why aren't they coming closer?"

70
00:03:44.788 --> 00:03:45.248
she muttered.

71
00:03:45.268 --> 00:03:48.009
"I know I did the right spell."

72
00:03:48.029 --> 00:03:51.590
"Maybe Darb could try to tame them," Zann suggested.

73
00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.271
"He's great with animals."

74
00:03:53.911 --> 00:03:55.472
Darb didn't respond for a second.

75
00:03:56.204 --> 00:03:58.286
He was still watching the hoof beasts carefully.

76
00:03:58.306 --> 00:04:01.208
"They look nervous," he said.

77
00:04:01.228 --> 00:04:04.531
"Actually they look scared."

78
00:04:04.551 --> 00:04:05.832
"Of us?"

79
00:04:06.393 --> 00:04:07.013
Perda wondered.

80
00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:13.078
"Why?" Before anyone could respond, one of the hoof beasts let out a sharp whistle.

81
00:04:13.779 --> 00:04:17.822
The entire herd wheeled around and galloped off across the sand.

82
00:04:17.842 --> 00:04:20.064
"Stop!" Wyssa cried.

83
00:04:20.745 --> 00:04:22.806
She flung magic energy after the animals.

84
00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:24.608
"Get back here!"

85
00:04:25.208 --> 00:04:27.090
But the beasts were already gone.

86
00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:30.533
"I wonder what scared them," Gliss said.

87
00:04:30.553 --> 00:04:35.997
"Maybe they Zann stopped as the sand rumbled beneath his feet.

88
00:04:36.898 --> 00:04:37.778
"What was that?"

89
00:04:38.599 --> 00:04:39.880
Perda took a step back.

90
00:04:40.721 --> 00:04:42.302
"The ground is moving!"

91
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:44.264
Zann glanced around.

92
00:04:44.864 --> 00:04:46.786
The sand was shifting everywhere he looked.

93
00:04:47.507 --> 00:04:50.909
A few dozen strides ahead, a sinkhole appeared to be forming.

94
00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:57.186
Suddenly sand shot upward as an enormous, lumpy head burst out of the ground!

95
00:04:57.906 --> 00:05:00.388
It looked almost like a dragon—but much bigger.

96
00:05:01.048 --> 00:05:06.751
Its snake-like neck was the same color as the sand, and its mouth held two rows of jagged

97
00:05:06.812 --> 00:05:09.133
teeth. "Oh, no!"

98
00:05:09.473 --> 00:05:10.274
Perda gasped.

99
00:05:10.294 --> 00:05:12.235
"It's a sand beast!"

100
00:05:12.255 --> 00:05:14.516
"What's a sand beast?"

101
00:05:14.776 --> 00:05:15.397
Gliss cried.

102
00:05:15.417 --> 00:05:17.098
"I'll tell you later."

103
00:05:17.778 --> 00:05:18.739
Perda spun around.

104
00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:20.900
"We have to get out of here!"

105
00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:24.519
She took off as fast as she could in the shifting sand.

106
00:05:25.179 --> 00:05:29.563
Zann raced after her and almost crashed into her when she skidded to a stop.

107
00:05:30.043 --> 00:05:34.427
The sand beast's forked tail had just emerged from the sand ahead of them!

108
00:05:35.508 --> 00:05:36.389
They spun around.

109
00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:40.752
But several legs with claws were popping into view all around them.

110
00:05:40.772 --> 00:05:44.676
"How many arms and legs does this thing have?"

111
00:05:45.056 --> 00:05:45.696
Gliss cried.

112
00:05:46.477 --> 00:05:48.259
"Enough," Darb said grimly.

113
00:05:48.679 --> 00:05:49.560
"We're surrounded!"

114
00:05:50.292 --> 00:05:53.673
The beast's giant head dived at Zann, and he ducked.

115
00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.914
Saliva sizzled as it hit the hot sand.

116
00:05:57.114 --> 00:05:58.834
"Gliss, look out!"

117
00:05:59.054 --> 00:05:59.655
Darb yelled.

118
00:06:00.715 --> 00:06:04.556
Zann spun around and saw one of the creature's claws moving toward Gliss.

119
00:06:05.256 --> 00:06:08.117
He snapped his fingers and sent a bolt of energy toward it.

120
00:06:08.737 --> 00:06:13.858
But instead of zipping toward the clawed arm, Zann's magic energy burst into a fireball!

121
00:06:14.579 --> 00:06:19.320
That distracted the sand beast just long enough for Gliss to dart away from its claws.

122
00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:22.550
Darb grabbed her and pulled her closer to the others.

123
00:06:23.251 --> 00:06:28.014
The group huddled together as the beast's multiple limbs all moved toward them.

124
00:06:29.375 --> 00:06:30.696
"We have to get out of here!"

125
00:06:31.037 --> 00:06:31.637
Zann cried.

126
00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:32.838
"Join hands!"

127
00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:35.040
"Don't try to zap!"

128
00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.021
Wyssa shouted.

129
00:06:36.041 --> 00:06:40.084
"Your magic will—" Zann didn't wait for her to finish.

130
00:06:40.784 --> 00:06:44.527
As soon as he and his friends were touching, he screamed, "Zap!"
